 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you doing? Start with small pile of wood that fits fully on fire stand. Roughly double it with well dried twigs and small branches. Then top it up with dry twigs and small branches. Yes, they make great kindling builders. Stick them between the layers of wood to make a deep pocket. Of course. Pop one in each pocket and you'll always find them at bedtime. Large enough to sit on with your legs on either side. Then a small but deep fire is enough. Put it on a flat rock or several layers of bricks so it's several inches above the cold ground. Also protect it from rain with a dry blanket.",
